    <string name="parent_level_title">English level</string>
    <string name="parent_level_hint">Level 1 to 7, for any age. It sets how Tuki talks: how long the answers are, whether mistakes get a named rule or a gentle repeat, and how much Hebrew help is offered. Hebrew fades as the level rises and is off at 6–7.</string>
    <string name="parent_level_hebrew_note">Hebrew explanations need the larger model (E4B), and are offered through Level 5 — at 6 and 7 the practice is English-only on purpose.</string>
    <string name="parent_gloss_title">Hebrew pronunciation</string>
    <string name="parent_gloss_hint">Shows how to say each English word, in Hebrew letters. Follows the level until you change it here.</string>
    <!-- Escaped on purpose: the nikud is invisible in an editor and gets
         silently reordered by anything that normalises this file. qof+segol+tet. -->
    <string name="parent_gloss_example">cat \u2192 \u05e7\u05b6\u05d8</string>
